IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cbr-nouns`
IMPORT `cbr-reg1`
IMPORT `cbr-reg2-benefits`
IMPORT `cbr-reg2-couples`

-- Child Benefit (Rates) Regulations 2006 -- LAYER 1, MODULE 5: REGULATION 2(1)
-- (the weekly rate: the enhanced rate and the rate in any other case) AND REGULATION
-- 2(4) (when the enhanced rate is not paid), with the composition of paragraphs (1)
-- to (5) that paragraph (1)(a) calls for ("subject to paragraphs (2) to (5)").
--
-- ORDER OF APPLICATION (fork F1, F2). The text states no priority among paragraphs
-- (2), (4) and (5): paragraph (1)(a) is "subject to" all three, paragraph (4) says
-- the enhanced rate "shall not be payable" in two cases, paragraph (5) says it "shall
-- be payable" in another, and paragraph (2) starts from what "would, but for this
-- paragraph, be payable ... at the enhanced rate". The order below is THE ENCODING'S,
-- chosen so that each step reads the result of the steps above it:
--   1. paragraph (1)(a): the child is the only, or the elder or eldest, child paid for;
--   2. paragraph (4) takes the enhanced rate away (voluntary organisation; living with
--      a parent of the child otherwise than as a couple);
--   3. paragraph (5) gives it back where a specified benefit is paid for the child;
--   4. paragraph (2), which takes "but for this paragraph" as its input, keeps it for
--      only the elder or eldest of the children of a couple or polygamous household.
-- Reading paragraph (4) above paragraph (5) instead would leave paragraph (5) with
-- nothing to do (it speaks of the same child as paragraph (1)(a)), which is why step 3
-- comes after step 2. Reordering the arms below changes the law this file states.
--
-- NOT COVERED, returned as NOTHING (never FALSE, never 0):
--   * a week that begins before these Regulations came into force (reg 1(1));
--   * a week that begins before the date of the version of the text encoded, because
--     the text dates neither figure (fork F8);
--   * a person who is neither a child nor a qualifying young person (reg 2(1) fixes a
--     rate "in respect of a child or qualifying young person" only);
--   * a child for whom child benefit is not payable at all (entitlement is the parent
--     Act's, out of text: reg 2(1) fixes the rate of child benefit "payable", so with
--     nothing payable it fixes no rate, and never a rate of 0);
--   * two children born on the same day, where the text does not say which is the
--     elder (fork F3).

§ `Regulation 2(1) and (4): the weekly rate`

§§ `Regulation 2(1): the two rates`

-- The text calls £27.05 "the enhanced rate" and gives £17.90 no name; amounts are
-- pounds a week.
-- src:19 | (a) subject to paragraphs (2) to (5), in a case where in any week a child or qualifying young person is the only person or, if not the only person, the elder or eldest person in respect of whom child benefit is payable to a person, £27.05 (“the enhanced rate”);
@ref reg 2(1)(a) (src:19)
`the enhanced rate` MEANS 27.05

-- src:20 | (b) in any other case, £17.90.
@ref reg 2(1)(b) (src:20)
`the rate in any other case` MEANS 17.90

-- The two figures are those of the version of the text encoded (fork F8).
-- src:19 | (a) subject to paragraphs (2) to (5), in a case where in any week a child or qualifying young person is the only person or, if not the only person, the elder or eldest person in respect of whom child benefit is payable to a person, £27.05 (“the enhanced rate”);
-- src:20 | (b) in any other case, £17.90.
@ref reg 2(1)(a), (b) (src:19-20)
GIVEN `first day of the week` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the figures in regulation 2(1) are those of the text in the week beginning` `first day of the week` MEANS
    `first day of the week` AT LEAST `the date of the version of the text encoded`

§§ `Regulation 2(1): in respect of a child or qualifying young person`

-- src:18 | (1) The weekly rate of child benefit payable in respect of a child or qualifying young person shall be—
@ref reg 2(1) (src:18)
GIVEN child IS A `Child or qualifying young person at the start of the week`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is a child or a qualifying young person` child MEANS
        child's `a child for the purposes of child benefit`
    OR  `a person is a qualifying young person for the purposes of these Regulations` (child's `where the young person is`) (child's `a qualifying young person for the purposes of Part 9 of SSCBA`) (child's `a qualifying young person for the purposes of Part 9 of SSCB(NI)A`)

§§ `Regulation 2(4): when child benefit is not payable at the enhanced rate`

-- src:32 | (4) Child benefit shall not be payable at the enhanced rate if the person to whom child benefit is payable is—
-- src:33 | (a) a voluntary organisation; or
@ref reg 2(4)(a) (src:32-33)
GIVEN claimant IS A `Claimant at the start of the week`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`paragraph (4)(a) applies to the claimant` claimant MEANS
    claimant's `a voluntary organisation`

-- src:34 | (b) a person residing (otherwise than as mentioned in paragraph (2)(a)) with a parent of the child or qualifying young person in respect of whom it is payable.
@ref reg 2(4)(b) (src:34)
GIVEN child IS A `Child or qualifying young person at the start of the week`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`paragraph (4)(b) applies to the claimant` child MEANS
        child's `the claimant resides with a parent of the child or qualifying young person`
    AND (NOT child's `the claimant resides with that parent as mentioned in paragraph (2)(a)`)

-- src:32 | (4) Child benefit shall not be payable at the enhanced rate if the person to whom child benefit is payable is—
-- src:33 | (a) a voluntary organisation; or
-- src:34 | (b) a person residing (otherwise than as mentioned in paragraph (2)(a)) with a parent of the child or qualifying young person in respect of whom it is payable.
@ref reg 2(4) (src:32-34)
GIVEN claimant IS A `Claimant at the start of the week`
      child IS A `Child or qualifying young person at the start of the week`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`paragraph (4) bars the enhanced rate` claimant child MEANS
        `paragraph (4)(a) applies to the claimant` claimant
    OR  `paragraph (4)(b) applies to the claimant` child

§§ `Regulation 2(1)(a): subject to paragraphs (2) to (5)`

-- Steps 1 to 3 of the order set out at the head of this module: the enhanced rate
-- that "would, but for [paragraph (2)], be payable".
-- src:19 | (a) subject to paragraphs (2) to (5), in a case where in any week a child or qualifying young person is the only person or, if not the only person, the elder or eldest person in respect of whom child benefit is payable to a person, £27.05 (“the enhanced rate”);
-- src:32 | (4) Child benefit shall not be payable at the enhanced rate if the person to whom child benefit is payable is—
-- src:33 | (a) a voluntary organisation; or
-- src:34 | (b) a person residing (otherwise than as mentioned in paragraph (2)(a)) with a parent of the child or qualifying young person in respect of whom it is payable.
-- src:35 | (5) If an allowance, or an increase of a benefit, pension or allowance, which is a specified benefit, is paid in respect of a week—
-- src:36 | (a) to a person, and
-- src:37 | (b) in respect of the only, elder or eldest child or qualifying young person in respect of whom that person is entitled to child benefit,
-- src:38 | child benefit shall be payable at the enhanced rate for that week.
@ref reg 2(1)(a), subject to paragraphs (4) and (5) (src:19, src:32-38)
GIVEN claimant IS A `Claimant at the start of the week`
      child IS A `Child or qualifying young person at the start of the week`
      payment IS A `Payment made for the week`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the enhanced rate would, but for paragraph (2), be payable for the child` claimant child payment MEANS
        child's `child benefit is payable to the claimant in respect of the child or qualifying young person`     -- "payable"
    AND child's `the only person, or the elder or eldest person, in respect of whom child benefit is payable to the claimant`     -- (1)(a)
    AND (   NOT (`paragraph (4) bars the enhanced rate` claimant child)                                                           -- (4) takes it away ...
         OR `paragraph (5) gives the enhanced rate for the child` payment child)                                                  -- ... and (5) gives it back

-- Step 4, with the gates: the Regulations in force, the figures known, a child or
-- qualifying young person. A child who is not one for whom the enhanced rate would be
-- payable is in "any other case" (paragraph (1)(b)).
-- src:18 | (1) The weekly rate of child benefit payable in respect of a child or qualifying young person shall be—
-- src:19 | (a) subject to paragraphs (2) to (5), in a case where in any week a child or qualifying young person is the only person or, if not the only person, the elder or eldest person in respect of whom child benefit is payable to a person, £27.05 (“the enhanced rate”);
-- src:20 | (b) in any other case, £17.90.
@ref reg 2(1) (src:18-20)
GIVEN `first day of the week` IS A DATE
      claimant IS A `Claimant at the start of the week`
      child IS A `Child or qualifying young person at the start of the week`
      payment IS A `Payment made for the week`
      others IS A `Other persons listed in paragraph (2)(a) at the start of the week`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Case under regulation 2(1)`
`the case under regulation 2(1) for the child in the week beginning` `first day of the week` claimant child payment others MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`these Regulations are in force in the week beginning` `first day of the week`) THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT (`the figures in regulation 2(1) are those of the text in the week beginning` `first day of the week`) THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT (`the person is a child or a qualifying young person` child) THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT (child's `child benefit is payable to the claimant in respect of the child or qualifying young person`) THEN NOTHING
        IF NOT (`the enhanced rate would, but for paragraph (2), be payable for the child` claimant child payment) THEN JUST `any other case`
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `paragraph (2) allows the enhanced rate for the claimant's child` claimant (child's `date of birth`) TRUE others
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST allowed THEN IF allowed THEN JUST `the case for the enhanced rate` ELSE JUST `any other case`

-- src:19 | (a) subject to paragraphs (2) to (5), in a case where in any week a child or qualifying young person is the only person or, if not the only person, the elder or eldest person in respect of whom child benefit is payable to a person, £27.05 (“the enhanced rate”);
-- src:20 | (b) in any other case, £17.90.
@ref reg 2(1)(a), (b) (src:19-20)
GIVEN regulation2case IS A `Case under regulation 2(1)`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the weekly rate in pounds for the case` regulation2case MEANS
    CONSIDER regulation2case
    WHEN `the case for the enhanced rate` THEN `the enhanced rate`
    WHEN `any other case` THEN `the rate in any other case`

-- src:18 | (1) The weekly rate of child benefit payable in respect of a child or qualifying young person shall be—
-- src:19 | (a) subject to paragraphs (2) to (5), in a case where in any week a child or qualifying young person is the only person or, if not the only person, the elder or eldest person in respect of whom child benefit is payable to a person, £27.05 (“the enhanced rate”);
-- src:20 | (b) in any other case, £17.90.
@ref reg 2(1) (src:18-20)
GIVEN `first day of the week` IS A DATE
      claimant IS A `Claimant at the start of the week`
      child IS A `Child or qualifying young person at the start of the week`
      payment IS A `Payment made for the week`
      others IS A `Other persons listed in paragraph (2)(a) at the start of the week`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the weekly rate of child benefit under regulation 2 for the child in the week beginning` `first day of the week` claimant child payment others MEANS
    CONSIDER `the case under regulation 2(1) for the child in the week beginning` `first day of the week` claimant child payment others
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST regulation2case THEN JUST (`the weekly rate in pounds for the case` regulation2case)
